	"notes": "This is Vue's own documentation, and it is the textbook three-column layout: a list of every page on the left, the article in the middle, and a table of contents for the CURRENT page on the right. What is worth knowing is what happens as the window gets very wide: past about 1920px the three columns stop growing and the whole group just floats in the middle of the screen with more empty space on both sides, the same way Wikipedia's article pages do — a 3440 ultrawide monitor does not get a wider article, it gets wider margins. On a phone both side columns vanish behind small buttons in the top bar (\"Menu\" and \"On this page\") rather than dropping underneath the article the way a simpler sidebar layout would, so getting to the navigation on a phone takes an extra tap.",
